{"title":"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pentagon is divided into 5 equal sections, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>An arrow is attached to the centre of the pentagon. The arrow is spun once. What is the probability that the arrow stops in the section numbered 4?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c3710223a867a7a47d88745db3850d513f7c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{3}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{4}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"371\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sections with equal probability and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> section numbered 4, so the probability of landing in the section numbered 4 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b27c6b4970c6e13c27ea6f0884b27daed4ebeda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } \\frac{1}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" tit